                "metadata": {
                    "description": "This free digital card was made by an Independent Creator and published on Yoto Space. Visit Open Mic on Yoto Space to discover more great free titles!  \n\nCreator: Lynnae Allred  \nFrom the Creator: “Baking chocolate chip cookies is fun—but thinking like a chef makes it an adventure! Discover the science behind baking and the incredible stories of the people who shaped the ingredients we use every day.   Dive into a fun-filled adventure that mixes step-by-step cookie baking instructions with mouthwatering science, and history! Follow every detail—from mise en place to the final golden cookie—and uncover the chemistry behind caramelization, leavening, creaming, and more.   \n\nAlong the way, meet culinary trailblazers like Ruth Wakefield, Joseph Dombey, Dr. Joseph Goldberger, and others who helped transform everyday ingredients into a legendary recipe loved all over the world. With humorous, engaging stories that show anyone can follow a recipe, but a chef creates one, this book inspires young bakers to explore, experiment, and think like a chef in every delicious moment.”  \n\nFor ages: 5-13   \n\nIf your family enjoyed this card, why not let the creator know by adding a comment on Open Mic?  \n\nFeatured on Discover until 1st December \nStays in your library and available on Yoto Space at any time",
